CONTEXT Library IN ENGLISH
PURPOSE CONTEXT Library
{+ The existing system of the migration cases, in production with this population.
Each declaration stands for one kind of item in section 4.1 of
"Data Migration under a Changing Schema in Ampersand" (RAMiCS 2024):
`title` is a relation that the desired system keeps, `shelf` one that it drops,
and `loan` one whose name it keeps with another signature.
The property [UNI] of `title` is a blocking invariant of both systems,
and `titled` one that only this system has. +}

RELATION title[Book*Title] [UNI]
RELATION shelf[Book*Shelf] [UNI]
RELATION loan[Book*Person]

RULE titled : I[Book] |- title;title~
MEANING "Every book has a title."

POPULATION title[Book*Title] CONTAINS [ ("b1", "Emma") ; ("b2", "Ivanhoe") ]
POPULATION shelf[Book*Shelf] CONTAINS [ ("b1", "S1") ]
POPULATION loan[Book*Person] CONTAINS [ ("b1", "Pete") ]

ENDCONTEXT
